#+title: Fang Doro Project Document

* Description:

Fang Doro is a pomodoro application that synchronizes with org mode todo features for another way to visualize the current to-do tasks with additional features, such as zen mode, where distraction-prone applications are blocked for the duration of a certain tasks (like blocking youtube, wikipedia).

It'll also have a GUI made in slint that synchronizes its colors with the desktop shell.
It's a simple timer for different tasks from org-todo and a blocker included.

* Tech Stack:

- Rust (Backend Logic) -> I want to learn Rust and I think this project is a good way for this since it's a program that I'm interested on and that I'll use probably on a daily basis.
- Slint (UI)

* Features:

** Early features:
- An user-defined timer (They can increase in intervals of 5 minutes or type in an arbitrary value)
- Breaks between focus time that are also user-defined
- Synchronizes with an user defined org file that contains TODO items
- Can define amount of slices for each task
- Timers can be defined separately for each task (e.g.: Task 1 has 25 minutes for focus while Task 2 has 40 minutes)

** Important features after initial implementation:
- Detect when a TODO item has a schedule, deadline, etc. and automatically add it to the UI
- Being able to select applications and websites that need to be blocked when a certain task's timer is started
- Block computer entirely if an IRL task needs to be done (ADHD much? /jk)
- Add autostart option for certain task

* Data structures:

** Org TODO item parser data type:
- Reads line with TODO header (Needs to be able to know all status of a TODO item)
- Checks a TODO item's priority
- Reads its title
- Reads keywords for Creation Date, Schedule, Deadline

** Timer data type:
- Needs to have an autoincrement option that can be user-defined
- User can define an arbitrary value for the timer
- Two 2 types of timer: Focus timers and Break timers (Both have the same features mentioned above)
- Play a sound and notify when a timer ends

** Undertemined data type:
- I dunno, lol.


* Auxiliary functions:

- A function that runs everytime the app starts, automatically syncing with the org file
- Functions to change timer attributes (Add amount of time, etc.)
- Function to change number of breaks
- Function to start blocking apps and websites when a timer starts
- Function that parses TODO items from todos.org
